  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Pittsburgh steamrolled the A's early and the game never tightened.",
    "what_this_means": "Aaron Civale couldn't survive three innings. Six runs crossed before anyone was recording outs, and by the second inning the deficit was already insurmountable. This is what happens when a starter implodes against a disciplined lineup. Pittsburgh saw fastballs and punished them. The bullpen held better (Suarez and Medina combined for four scoreless innings after Barlow's collapse in the fourth), but there was no rope to grab from down 10. They scraped together two runs in the sixth when it was already decided. Twelve strikeouts from a lineup that managed six hits is not a night that gets replayed. The inconsistency that has defined this season showed up again. A starter failing early, the offense unable to answer. This only works until it doesn't.",
    "what_to_watch": "LAA sends a TBD starter tonight at 6:40 PM. Gage Jump takes the mound with a 3.12 ERA over his last four starts, which is the kind of stability this team needs.",
